Problem
The 0G chat service was working but always falling back to local mode instead of attempting to use real 0G AI providers. Users experienced:

Direct fallback: provider 0xf07240Efa67755B5311bc75784a061eDB47165Dd failed: execution reverted: ServiceNotExist(address)
=== Chat Response (Direct) ===
Success: true, Model: fallback, Provider: local, Is Real AI: false
Root Causes:

Missing DirectChatService implementation (referenced in API route but not created)
Poor service discovery fallback when contract queries fail with "ServiceNotExist" errors
No fallback to hardcoded provider endpoints when contract discovery fails
Inadequate error handling for provider registration issues
Solution
1. Implemented DirectChatService
Created web/lib/compute/direct-chat-service.ts to provide proper fallback behavior:

